+        LISTEN run is skipped; the hand-off starts after ``<|tts_bos|>`` when
+        the unit has one (``tts_bos_offset``: the index right after it, 0 when
+        it was folded as the last prompt token), otherwise (``NO_TTS_BOS``)
+        after the unit's first decision token, and ends before the chunk
+        terminator, or after ``<|turn_eos|>``. ``None`` means it is not known
+        whether a ``<|tts_bos|>`` was folded into the prompt: the span is then
+        taken as if it was (the larger hand-off), so a caller asking whether
+        the Talker gets nothing only gets "nothing" when that holds either way.
+        Returns ``(unit_start, start, end, segment_end)`` (``segment_end``: a
+        chunk terminator closed it), or ``None`` when the
